Usage: agent-deck session send-status <send-id> [--no-resume] [--json]

State of a `session send --queue` message: queued, typing, typed, submitted, landed or failed,
with reason, target_status, attempts, and landed_row_id/landed_at once the text is
in the transcript (the row id recall timeline/follow use). Exit 0 when found, 2 for an unknown id.

landed is reported only on transcript evidence (a user row, or a queued message absorbed
into the turn). failed means this send typed nothing; use redeliver to check before reopening it.
Another send or manual input may already contain the same text. A send whose outcome
could not be proven settles as typed/submitted (settled: true) and is never typed again.
  -json
    	Output as JSON
  -no-resume
    	Read the snapshot without starting a worker
